From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:06:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] backports: support the older USB device driver member

Keep the device_driver member required by brcmfmac when building against
kernels older than 6.8.

Original author was not recorded in the imported patch.
[viking.yfy@qq.com: complete imported patch metadata]
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/usb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/usb.c
@@ -1588,7 +1588,11 @@ static int brcmf_usb_reset_device(struct
 
 void brcmf_usb_exit(void)
 {
+#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_GEQ(6,8,0)
 	struct device_driver *drv = &brcmf_usbdrvr.driver;
+#else
+	struct device_driver *drv = &brcmf_usbdrvr.drvwrap.driver;
+#endif
 	int ret;
 
 	brcmf_dbg(USB, "Enter\n");
